Create a production-ready web application called "Test Data Sheet Builder".

Technology Requirements:
- HTML5
- CSS3
- Vanilla JavaScript ES6 modules
- SheetJS (xlsx library)
- GitHub Pages compatible
- No backend
- All processing performed in-browser
- Mobile responsive
- Local storage support
- Dark mode

Purpose:
Teachers create Excel marking spreadsheets for exams and tests.

Core Features:

STEP 1 – TEST DETAILS
- Input test name
- Name becomes workbook filename
- Name appears on every student feedback sheet

STEP 2 – STUDENTS
- Enter student count
- Paste student list
- Support:
  - Excel copied cells
  - TSV
  - CSV
- Store:
  - First name
  - Last name
  - Optional level
- Optional level heading

STEP 3 – QUESTIONS
- Unlimited questions
- Each question has:
  - Label
  - Marks available
- Auto numbering
- Renumber button
- Bulk mark assignment
- Multiple choice section option
- Running total marks

STEP 4 – MARKING CODES

Default:
Y = full marks

Teacher can create:
D = definition missing
A = analysis weak
C = calculation error

Rules:
Y on a 5-mark question = 5

DD on a 5-mark question = 3

DAC on a 6-mark question = 3

Invalid codes highlighted red

STEP 5 – GRADE BOUNDARIES

Default IB scale:

0 = 0
20 = 1
30 = 2
40 = 3
50 = 4
60 = 5
70 = 6
80 = 7

Editable by teacher.

